        "id": 5230
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T20:37:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC WrapAndroidHardwareBuffer takes the AHardwareBuffer* and wraps it with GrAHardwareBufferUtils::MakeBackendTexture. That call returns function pointers to do the deletion. Those are then fed into SkSurfaces::WrapBackendTexture so the backing memory will be cleaned up when possible (i.e., sometime after the SkSurface has been deleted). For GL, I believe the magic happens in AHardwareBufferGL.cpp GLTextureHelper - which refs and unrefs the AHardwareBuffer.",
      "parentUuid": "89075a75_f9906e4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "b96fe79c15b488e1855875173fc1d69f8fb3e899",
