      "writtenOn": "2023-08-15T15:18:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Best I can tell, outside of tests, Skia only *directly* acquires or releases an `AHardwareBuffer` in `GrAHardwareBufferImageGenerator`, which is created by `DeferredFromAHardwareBuffer`.\n\nI was getting nervous, but then I came across [this comment](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/ac2ba5d4d9d1c58212d596e4695ab36d4e0e8fb5:frameworks/base/libs/hwui/DeferredLayerUpdater.cpp;l\u003d174;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0), telling us that \n\n```\n// ... eglCreateImageKHR (invoked by createIfNeeded) will add a ref to the\n// AHardwareBuffer.\n```\n, and it looks like Vulkan\u0027s version, `VkImportAndroidHardwareBufferInfoANDROID`, [does the same](https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/1.3-extensions/man/html/VkImportAndroidHardwareBufferInfoANDROID.html).\n\nCircling back, `GrAHardwareBufferUtils::MakeBackendTexture` is called by `WrapAndroidHardwareBuffer`, so they get an acquire + release. So we still need to call `AHardwareBuffer_release` to account for the initial ref count of 1 provided by `AHardwareBuffer_allocate`.\n\nYou\u0027re doing that now, but I think it\u0027d be cleaner to release inside your new `CreateAHBBackedSurface`, after you\u0027ve called `WrapAndroidHardwareBuffer`, which takes its own ref.",
      "parentUuid": "d55afbee_f7d9e102",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "b96fe79c15b488e1855875173fc1d69f8fb3e899",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
